14 0 obj
<</Parent 19 0 R/Next 15 0 R/Prev 13 0 R/Title(The bar plot illustrates the distribution of caste categories across different geographical zones. Each bar represents a zone, and the segments within the bars represent the proportion of each caste category within that zone. The percentages displayed on top of each segment indicate the proportion of that caste category in relation to the total population of the respective zone. From the plot, we can observe that certain zones have a higher concentration of specific caste categories. For instance, the North zone has a higher percentage of General caste, while the South zone has a higher percentage of OBC. The Central and East zones show a more balanced distribution across caste categories. This visualization helps us understand the demographic composition of each geographical zone in terms of caste distribution.)/Dest 903 0 R>>
endobj
15 0 obj
<</Parent 19 0 R/Next 16 0 R/Prev 14 0 R/Title(PLOT 2 : plot the Distribution of per capita income across zones)/Dest 904 0 R>>
endobj
16 0 obj
