endobj
17 0 obj
<</Parent 18 0 R/Title(Final Check)/Dest 907 0 R>>
endobj
18 0 obj
<</Parent 19 0 R/Prev 16 0 R/First 17 0 R/Last 17 0 R/Count -1/Title(The boxplot illustrates the distribution of per capita income across different geographical zones. The median income is represented by the line within each box, while the boxes themselves show the interquartile range (IQR). The whiskers extend to 1.5 times the IQR, and any points beyond that are considered outliers. From the plot, we can observe that the North and South zones have higher median incomes compared to the Central and East zones. Additionally, the West zone shows a wider spread of income, indicating greater variability in per capita income within that zone. Outliers are present in all zones, suggesting that there are some households with significantly higher or lower incomes than the majority.)/Dest 906 0 R>>
endobj
