<</Type/Catalog/Pages 1 0 R/Metadata 959 0 R/PageLabels 20 0 R/Lang(en-US)/StructTreeRoot 21 0 R/MarkInfo<</Marked true/Suspects false>>/ViewerPreferences<</Direction/L2R>>/Outlines 19 0 R/Names<</Dests<</Names[(assessment-environment)894 0 R(final-check)907 0 R(ihds-data-exercise)893 0 R(interpretatiion-of-the-above-plot)902 0 R(interpretation-of-the-above-plot)905 0 R(load-required-libraries)892 0 R(plot-1-caste-distribution-across-zones)901 0 R(plot-2-plot-the-distribution-of-per-capita-income-across-zones)904 0 R(question-1-data-cleaning-and-visualization)895 0 R(setup)891 0 R(step-1)896 0 R(step-2)897 0 R(step-3-create-new-variable-for-geographical-zones)898 0 R(step-4-clean-data-by-removing-rows-with-missing-values-in-key-variables)899 0 R(step-5-contingency-table---caste-vs-zones)900 0 R(the-bar-plot-illustrates-the-distribution-of-caste-categories-across-different-geographical-zones.-each-bar-represents-a-zone-and-the-segments-within-the-bars-represent-the-proportion-of-each-caste-category-within-that-zone.-the-percentages-displayed-on-top-of-each-segment-indicate-the-proportion-of-that-caste-category-in-relation-to-the-total-population-of-the-respective-zone.-from-the-plot-we-can-observe-that-certain-zones-have-a-higher-concentration-of-specific-caste-categories.-for-instance-the-north-zone-has-a-higher-percentage-of-general-caste-while-the-south-zone-has-a-higher-percentage-of-obc.-the-central-and-east-zones-show-a-more-balanced-distribution-across-caste-categories.-this-visualization-helps-us-understand-the-demographic-composition-of-each-geographical-zone-in-terms-of-caste-distribution.)903 0 R(the-boxplot-illustrates-the-distribution-of-per-capita-income-across-different-geographical-zones.-the-median-income-is-represented-by-the-line-within-each-box-while-the-boxes-themselves-show-the-interquartile-range-iqr.-the-whiskers-extend-to-1.5-times-the-iqr-and-any-points-beyond-that-are-considered-outliers.-from-the-plot-we-can-observe-that-the-north-and-south-zones-have-higher-median-incomes-compared-to-the-central-and-east-zones.-additionally-the-west-zone-shows-a-wider-spread-of-income-indicating-greater-variability-in-per-capita-income-within-that-zone.-outliers-are-present-in-all-zones-suggesting-that-there-are-some-households-with-significantly-higher-or-lower-incomes-than-the-majority.)906 0 R]>>>>>>
